<%# The summary a guest agrees to before anything reaches the hotel.
    The element is always rendered, empty when there is nothing pending,
    because it is the target of a Turbo replace from
    ServiceRequestDraft#broadcast_card — a target that does not exist yet is
    a broadcast that lands nowhere.

    Both buttons post to the guest's own live draft with no id in the form:
    there is nothing tenant- or record-identifying anywhere in this
    namespace's routes, and this card does not invent an exception just
    because a form could technically carry one. Confirm converges on the
    same ServiceRequestDraft#confirm! a typed "yes" reaches through the
    model, which is what makes it impossible for the two paths to produce
    two requests. %>
<div id="draft-card" class="px-4 pb-2">
  <% if draft %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border-2 p-3" style="border-color:var(--brand-primary)" role="group"
         aria-labelledby="draft-card-heading">
      <p id="draft-card-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900" dir="auto">
        <%= t("requests.card.heading") %>
      </p>

      <p id="draft-card-summary" class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-800" dir="auto"><%= draft.summary_for_guest %></p>

      <% if draft.conversation.room %>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-gray-500" dir="auto">
          <%= t("requests.card.room", room: draft.conversation.room.number) %>
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <%# Said in words on the card itself, not only in the assistant's
          message: this is the one place the guest is agreeing to something,
          and "pending until a person acts" has to be legible right where
          the decision is made. %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500" dir="auto"><%= t("requests.card.pending_note") %></p>

      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <%= button_to t("requests.card.confirm"), confirm_guest_service_request_draft_path,
              id: "draft-confirm",
              class: "cursor-pointer rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white",
              style: "background-color:var(--brand-primary);color:var(--brand-on-primary)" %>

        <%# "Change" only fills the composer — the same chip behaviour the
            quick actions use — so changing your mind is always a sentence
            you type, never a form this app guessed at on your behalf. %>
        <button type="button" id="draft-change" dir="auto"
                class="rounded-full border px-4 py-1.5 text-sm"
                style="border-color:var(--brand-secondary)"
                data-action="click->chat-composer#fillFromChip"
                data-prefill-text="<%= t('requests.card.change_prefill') %>">
          <%= t("requests.card.change") %>
        </button>

        <%= button_to t("requests.card.cancel"), discard_guest_service_request_draft_path,
              id: "draft-cancel",
              class: "cursor-pointer rounded-full border border-gray-300 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
